4. Analyze the results: The output of the PCA will include a list of principal coordinates, which are ordered by significance. The first few principal coordinates typically explain the most variation in the data. Analyze the eigenvectors and their coefficients to determine which environmental factors are most significant in explaining the growth of the bacteria.

