Oxalyine compounds in *Oxalus corniculata* (also known as ""Texasylo"" or ""sourwood"") are not effective for treating indigestion in cattle. Oxalic acid, a compound in this plant, can be harmful to birds and animals, causing kidney damage and necrosis. In cattle, it can lead to kidney damage and necrosis, which can be fatal. Therefore, *Oxalus corniculata* should not be used to treat indigestion or any other ailment in patients.

