- Guanine (G): 25 (on the single strand) × 2 = 50 in the double-stranded molecule.
- Cytosine (C): 30 (on the single strand) × 2 = 60 in the double-stranded molecule.
- Thymine (T): 22 (on the single strand) × 2 = 44 in the double-stranded molecule.

So, the complete double-stranded DNA molecule contains 40 A, 50 G, 60 C, and 44 T.

