3. Prepare a known amount of activated carbon.
4. Add a fixed amount of activated carbon to each water sample and mix thoroughly.
5. Allow the activated carbon-water mixture to come into contact for different time intervals (e.g., 10, 30, 60, and 90 minutes).
6. Filter the mixture to separate the activated carbon from the water.
