5. **Mostius-Meerwein reaction:** This reaction involves the conversion of the chiral alcohol to a diastereomeric ester, which can be easily resolved by column chromatography. The recovered ester can then be hydrolyzed to regenerate the chiral alcohol, and its configuration can be determined by comparing its properties to those of the known R or S enantiomer.

