   - Assume 108 g of the compound.
   - The mass of each element in the compound is:
     - Carbon (C): \( \frac{9}{7.5} \times 108 = 122 \) g
     - Hydrogen (H): \( \frac{1}{7.5} \times 108 = 14.4 \) g
     - Nitrogen (N): \( \frac{3.5}{7.5} \times 108 = 51.4 \) g
   - Convert the mass of each element to moles:
     - Moles of C: \( \frac{122}{12} = 10 \) mol
     - Moles of H: \( \frac{14.4}{1} = 14.4 \) mol
     - Moles of N: \( \frac{51.4}{14} = 3.5 \) mol
