Compound ‘A’ (molecular formula C₅H₁₂O) is treated with acidified potassium dichromate to form a product ‘B’ (molecular formula C₅H₁₀O). ‘B’ forms a shining silver mirror on warming with ammonical silver nitrate. ‘B’ when treated with an aqueous solution of sodium hydroxide liberates gas ‘C’. Identify A, B, and C.<end_of_turn>
