","Let the cost price of the article be \( R \).  
Let the marked price be \( M \).  
Given:  
After deducting 10% from the list price, it is spoken at a profit of 25% on the cost price.  
\[
M - 0.10M = 1.25R \implies 0.9M = 1.25R \implies M = \frac{1.25}{0.9}R = \frac{25}{18}R
\]  
