","To prove this, we use the definition of a polyhedral cone and the properties of linear hyperplanes.

1. **Existence of the Hyperplane**:
   - The cone \( C \) is defined as the set of all linear combinations of \( a_1, \ldots, a_n \) with nonnegative coefficients.
   - The set \( \text{span}(a_1, \ldots, a_n)\} \) is the set of all linear combinations of \( a_1, \ldots, a_n \), which spans the span of the vectors \( a_1, \ldots, a_n \).
