","1. **Calculate the total area of the rectangular courtyard:**  
   \[
   \text{Area} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} = 50 \text{ m} \times 16.5 \text{ m} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

2. **Calculate the area of one paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Area of one stone} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width}
   \]

3. **Set up an proportion to find the width of the paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Area of one stone} \times \text{Number of stamps} = \text{Total area}
   \]  
   \[
   2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width} \times 165 = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Solve for the width of the paving stone:**  
   \[
   2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width} = \frac{825}{165} = 4.75 \text{ m}
   \]  
   \[
   \text{Width} = \frac{4.75}{2.5} = 1.9 \text{ m}
   \]

   The width of each paving stone is \(\boxed{1.9 \text{ m}}\).
