","1. **Calculate the distance A travels before B starts:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance by A} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 10 \, \text{kmph} \times 3 \, \text{years} = 30 \, \text{km}
   \]

2. **Determine the relative speed of B with respect to A:**  
   \[
   \text{Relative speed} = \text{Speed of B} - \text{Speed of A} = 20 \, \text{kmph} - 10 \, \text{kmph} = 10 \, \text{kmph}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time it takes B to cover the distance A has traveled:**  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{30 \, \text{km}}{10 \, \text{kmph}} = 3 \, \text{years}
   \]

4. **Determine the distance B covers to catch A:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance by B} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 20 \, \text{kmph} \times 3 \, \text{years} = 60 \, \text{km}
   \]

5. **Calculate the distance from the start where B cancels up with A:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance from start} = 30 \, \text{km} + 60 \, \text{km} = 90 \, \text{km}
   \]

\[
\boxed{90 \, \text{km}}
\]
