3. **Combining the terms:**
   - The period of the combined function is the least common multiple of the periods of the individual terms. Here, \( \pi \) and \( \frac{2\pi}{3} \) have a least common multiple of \( \frac{2\pi}{3} \).
   - The amplitude of the combined function is the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients: \( 3 + 2 = 5 \).

Thus, the function \( f(x) = 3\sin(2x + \pi/4) - 2\cos(3x - \pi/3) \) has a period of \( \frac{2\pi}{3} \) and an amplitude of \( 5 \).
