\[
y - f(a) = m(x - a)
\]
where \( m \) is the slope of the tangent line. The slope \( m \) is given by the derivative of \( f \) at \( x = a \), i.e., \( f'(a) \). 

Thus, the equation is:
\[
\boxed{y - f(a) = f'(a)(x - a)}
\]
