\]
The limit \( \lim_{x \to 0} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) \) is \( \frac{\pi}{2} \) as \( \frac{1}{x} \to \infty \). Thus, \( f'(0) = \frac{\pi}{2} \).
Since the derivative \( f'(0) \) exists, the function \( f(x) \) is differentiable at \( x = 0 \).

