\]
Subtract \( \frac{13}{15}x \) from both sides:
\[
14 = \frac{2}{15}x
\]
Multiply both sides by \( \frac{15}{2} \):
\[
x = 14 \times \frac{15}{2} = 105 \text{ kilometers}
\]
Thus, the distance from the dormitory to the city is \(\boxed{105 \text{ kilometers}}\).

