\[
d = 500 \text{ Å} = 500 \times 10^{-10} \text{ m}
\]

Now, compute the depletion layer capacitance per unit area:
\[
C_d = \frac{4 \times 9.8 \times 10^9}{500 \times 10^{-10}} = 7.84 \times 10^{-12} \text{ F/m}^2
\]

The problem states that the threshold voltage shifts by \(-1.0\) V. Thus:
