","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T}
\]
where \( Q \) is the rate of heat transfer. The heat transfer is due to the work done by the friction force \( F_{\text{fr}} \) over the relative velocity \( v \). The work done by friction is:
\[
dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]
The heat transfer \( Q \) is equal to the work done by friction:
\[
Q = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is \( \boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}} \).
