   \]  
   where \(Pr\) is the Prandtl number. For air at 500°C, \(Pr \approx 0.0001\). Substituting the values:  
   \[
   Nu = 0.004 \times 40,000^{0.25} \times 0.0001^{0.7} \approx 0.004
